# Performance Diagram Example

This example demonstrates how to aggregate CTS (contingency table statistics) data from
MET stat files and plot it as a performance diagram using VCasT. It uses `RRFS_mem000`
1-hr accumulated precipitation (APCP_01, >0.0 mm) and plots probability of detection
(PODY) against 1 - false alarm ratio (1-FAR), with background contours for frequency bias
and critical success index (CSI).

## Data Aggregation:
This step processes the MET CTS stat files and aggregates PODY/FAR/CSI/FBIAS/GSS into an
output file for plotting.

## Plot Generation:
This step uses the aggregated output file to draw the performance diagram.

## Commands

1. Aggregate Data
Run the following command to process the MET stat files. This produces `APCP01_agg.data`,
aggregated by model/fcst_var/fcst_lead.

```bash
# Aggregates MET CTS stat files and creates the aggregated data file
vcast cts.yaml
```

2. Generate the Performance Diagram
Once the data aggregation is complete, run the following command to generate the diagram
using the aggregated data:

```bash
# Generates the performance diagram using the aggregated output file
vcast plot.yaml
```
